    "name": "a kill cancels an automatic delivery retry and fails the send retryably"
  },
  "baselineRevision": "720aa48c5537cba0a25c00b65b59504437378886",
  "sourceSha256": {
    "baseline": "068605fc9e9f0ca4d18bc566e7b98d8a7d34e9717a93ae8d43b5268dd13b79ed",
    "fixed": "1439b481c7536116ae25e89dfc2199bbdcbc3bacce7f56ab168a88c963dc72f2"
  },
  "classification": "Test ordering assumptions",
  "cause": [
    "A startup observation can already be waiting in the controller when the send is admitted. It can drain that send in addition to the route kick, producing four send calls instead of two.",
    "The scheduled observation after the kill has no 100 ms completion guarantee. Sampling before it reads the retained kill boundary produces an additional effect read during the asserted quiet interval.",
    "The route-kick error printed immediately before the CI failure belongs to the preceding test; the kill case reproduces alone."
  ],
  "fix": [
    "Join startup through a fresh-admission kick before admitting any send.",
    "Use the same fresh-admission kick as the production message route.",
    "Wait for an effect read containing only retained kill boundaries after the kill is delivered and the send has failed, then join that drain before sampling quietness."
  ],
